    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14046",
      "problem": "Sketch the solution to the inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/c3ff3eee7734c983d2915acb172cf1ae2173611edf5e11bf2228a0d2bc1b687d.svg).",
      "worked_solution": "First, we draw the corresponding straight line  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/afc3f4a4e0950030b20e41f58cf4d90734a6d8dd6577fd46df86ae00c12bf6b1.svg) Since the inequality involves a 'strictly less than' sign, the line  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/18af1222b10f1042254cf589e52bf81f603fb29f14428343b2bbd9dfff7c7bf6.svg) itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **dashed line.**\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/75f17da6637e696cd97d49d844818bb0810bbf7abc4a0507ac72dbe4b0a3ceb0.png)\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/c3ff3eee7734c983d2915acb172cf1ae2173611edf5e11bf2228a0d2bc1b687d.svg) refers to the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-values that are *less than* those on the line ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/9181ac4b69f87417e52f691a281329f2198fac06b1e05e7fa9f764d2a3448d09.svg) so we shade *below* the line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/028835cf1d5ad49c29f69bfd7cdf7a716d8fa1b613a7990f9ee4e0f034337ee0.png)\n\nLet's now check that we've shaded the correct part. First, we consider a point in the shaded region, say ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/897570ce172a9f169127c297c355bc7a446b1df6ee78afe238f5b53dde75a85c.svg)  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/e5d1d1c281f864ba901fcae5a980920e155cc19b48a5d73f80546d519837aec2.png)\n\n \n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates of this point into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/2fa1aaea0475b048dda780feed23f5e9157972f6a5eeed5567f06aa1a5968d88.svg) \n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region.",
